    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0375" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/6–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-03T21:00:00+08:00">June 3, 1949—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 4—12:38 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 529. Legislative Yuan approved Yen Hsi-shan as premier this morning by 254
                    to 56 with 10 ballots invalid. Entire process took only little over 1 hour
                    including half-hour insipid pro-Yen speeches. Few scattered handclaps when
                    results announced.</p>
                <p>Easy majority favoring Yen probably accounted for by: (1) C–C Clique satisfied
                    Yen definitely not hostile toward Gimo;<anchor n="83" xml:id="d431-f1"/> (2)
                    Legislative <pb facs="0376" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/> Yuan anxiety recess for
                    summer and board ships now awaiting take them Formosa. Interesting to note that
                    Yen flew Formosa yesterday ostensibly to bury mother.</p>
                <p>Sent Department Cantel 529; repeated Nanking 360; Shanghai 307.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d431-f1" n="83" xml:id="d431-f1-content">
                <p>Generalissimo Chiang Kai-Shek, who retired as President of the Republic of China
                    on January 21, 1949.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
